      "translation": "What I have said so far corresponds to the first part of this lecture, but I am thinking of moving on to the second part. Gakushuin is viewed by the public as a school for people of good social standing. So that's probably true. If, as I have surmised, the poor people do not come here, but rather only the children of the upper classes gather here, then the first thing that will come with you in the future is power. In other words, when you go out into the world, you have more power than if you were a poor person. As I mentioned earlier, working and moving forward until you find something is for your happiness and peace of mind, but the reason why it brings you happiness and peace of mind is because you only settle down when your innate individuality collides with it. This is probably because if you settle down and move forward gradually, your individuality will develop more and more. It is only when your work and your individuality are a perfect fit that you can say that this is where I found my safe place."
